Certified nursing assistant (CNA)

Organisation
The care in the Netherlands is innovative and continuously evolving, known internationally for its efficiency, quality and personal attention for both patient and care professional. Due to the open culture, international careers and nurses are welcome in the Netherlands for an exciting career.

Zorg groep Beek supports you as a care professional in finding long-term employment with the most renowned nursing and care organizations in the Netherlands. Zorg groep Beek offers you:
Professional guidance throughout the recruitment process
- Personal assessment
- Dutch language schooling, A2 level
- Practical support: BSN (citizen service number), accommodation, transport
- Accreditation of diplomas and registration with the right registers
A workplace with a suitable care institution, which immediately becomes your employer and with which you sign a direct employment contract.
Guidance with your employer for 3 years, with your own community, training, coaching and practical matters.
HiNurse: Follow your passion abroad.

We are looking for enthusiastic Care assistants EQF 3 for the provision of care in the care departments of nursing and care homes in the province of Limburg, Netherlands.

Care assistant EQF 3
Job description
The activities with the patients are varied and comprise, among other things:
- caring for, nursing and guiding the clients in accordance with the life care plans;
- (under supervision) drawing up or adjusting life care plans in accordance with the needs of the client;
- coordinating the provision of care and services within a care department;
- monitoring and promoting the quality and quantity of care provided;
- liaising with and collaborating with the care coordinator;
- issuing and administering medicines.
Requirements
You must have a passion for the provision of top quality care, paying sincere attention to the client!
Besides this, as a candidate we seek from you:
- strong communication and social skills;
- care assistant diploma - EQF 3;
- English level B1;
- a strong sense of responsibility and empathy;
- demonstrating initiative and creativity in proposing solutions;
- working in accordance with the ruling norms and quality standards.
What we offer
- employment contract with a permanent contract;
- excellent employment conditions and salary in accordance with the collective labour agreement for the care sector (CAO VVT);
- friendly colleagues;
- Professional care organisation committed to a pleasant working atmosphere and job satisfaction;
- Possibilities for schooling and for growth and development.

Heerema Fabrication Group is located in the harbour of Vlissingen, Southwest of the Netherlands. The company is looking for welders. You will be working at the Heerema Vlissingen yard in Vlissingen.

You are responsible for welding activities on projects such as the new construction of offshore structures.

Responsibilities:
You can independently perform high-standard welding work with carbon steel. (e.g. S235 - S460) with wall thicknesses varying from 3 to 130 mm);
Welding processes FCAW(138) and FCAW(136) for both full penetration welds as well as fillet welds;
Welding in various positions and according to project-specific procedures (‘WPS’);
Extensive experience in gouging;
Contribute to a safe and efficient working environment.

Education and experience:
Vocational level, supported with function-specific courses;
At least five years of experience as a welder;
Valid welding certificates conform EN-ISO 9606-1 (and optional EN-287-1 and AWS D1.1);
Valid Basic Safety VCA;
Willingness to work in shifts (and overtime if necessary);
Good command of Dutch and/or English language.

For this position we require the following skills and characteristics:

• Working safely is very important to you and you know how to convey this to other employees;
• You work well in a team;
• Good communication skills;
• You are flexible and have a hands-on mentality.
